  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "How it scales",
      "items": [
        "API: stateless tasks, desired_count is a Terraform variable; ALB spreads across both AZs.",
        "Worker: N tasks claim disjoint outbox batches via SKIP LOCKED and compete for SQS messages; a lease per event_id keeps duplicates out.",
        "Throughput ceiling today: 25 outbox rows per poll, poll serialized behind a 10 s SQS long-poll; split poller and consumer roles to lift it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Failure domains",
      "items": [
        "RDS single-AZ is the only durable state; a failover is a restart, not data loss (outbox rows survive).",
        "Redis loss: cache misses and a degraded live stream, no data impact.",
        "Worker outage: SQS buffers up to 14 days; EventBridge retries 24 times for 1 h, then the target DLQ.",
        "Poison message: left in queue, redriven after 5 receives; attempt_number >= 5 emits event.processing.failed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Deliberate Phase-1 trade-offs",
      "items": [
        "Tasks sit in public subnets with public IPs to avoid NAT cost; security groups admit only the ALB.",
        "Single region, single RDS AZ, HTTP-only ALB until TLS lands; scale-to-zero keeps cost near $40/month at rest.",
        "Secrets Manager and ECR edges are drawn once; every task in both AZs uses them."
      ]
    }
  ]
}